<article class="env-lemma" id="07NT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07NT">Lemma <span data-tag="07NT">15.42.7</span>.</a> Let $A \to B \to C$ be ring maps. If $A \to C$ is regular and $B \to C$ is flat and surjective on spectra, then $A \to B$ is regular. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/039V" data-tag="039V">10.39.10</a> we see that $A \to B$ is flat. Let $\mathfrak p \subset A$ be a prime. The ring map $B \otimes _ A \kappa (\mathfrak p) \to C \otimes _ A \kappa (\mathfrak p)$ is flat and surjective on spectra. Hence $B \otimes _ A \kappa (\mathfrak p)$ is geometrically regular by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/07NH" data-tag="07NH">10.166.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>